## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to craft a concrete, beginner-friendly CI gate that enforces per-container resource budgeting and a basic security posture—practical patterns seen in production.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes manifest traversal
- GitHub Actions CI gates
- resources.requests/limits
- securityContext basics (readOnlyRootFilesystem, allowPrivilegeEscalation)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js pseudo-check using js-yaml
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const path = './manifests';
for (const f of fs.readdirSync(path)) {
  if (!f.endsWith('.yaml')) continue;
  const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path + '/' + f, 'utf8'));
  const containers = (doc?.spec?.template?.spec?.containers) || [];
  for (const c of containers) {
    if (!c.resources?.requests || !c.resources?.limits) fail();
    if (c.securityContext?.readOnlyRootFilesystem !== true) fail();
    if (c.securityContext?.allowPrivilegeEscalation !== false) fail();
  }
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle multi-namespace repos?
- How would you surface results in PR checks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical detection pipeline for cloud-native DNS tunneling, combining kernel telemetry, DNS-layer analytics, and service-mesh visibility; emphasizes real-world validation and false-positive control.

## Key Concepts
- eBPF DNS egress monitoring
- CoreDNS analytics and entropy-based signals
- Istio telemetry integration and namespace scoping
- Multi-signal alerting and validation
- Synthetic traffic to verify detections

## Code Example
```javascript
function entropy(s){
  const counts = {};
  for(const ch of s) counts[ch]=(counts[ch]||0)+1;
  const total = s.length;
  let e=0; for(const c of Object.values(counts)){ const p=c/total; e -= p*Math.log2(p); }
  return e;
}
function isSuspicious(domain){
  const parts = domain.split('.');
  const labels = parts.slice(0,-1);
  const ent = labels.map(l=>entropy(l)).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  const len = domain.length;
  return ent>3.5 || len>30;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune thresholds to reduce false positives across tenants?
- What data retention and RBAC would you implement for CoreDNS and eBPF telemetry?
